  "findings": [],
  "id": "final-consolidation-code-review",
  "independence_basis": "Parent /root authored implementation, test adaptations, Design consolidation and plan. This reviewer authored none of those engineering contributions. Prior independent milestone and Design reviews provide attributable context; this invocation freshly assesses the complete delivered diff and cross-milestone/documentation interactions rather than reusing an earlier final judgment.",
  "judgment": "approved",
  "limitations": [
    "Final Verify must independently assess the complete required authority, proof, concern and closeout chain and record success only if warranted. This review does not claim branch readiness, PR readiness, Verify success or publication.",
    "Retirement-specific behavior is assessed statically under the explicit no-new-tests/no-manual-substitutes constraint. Existing supported/shared tests and final candidate composition evidence do not establish exhaustive retired-input coverage.",
    "Local CI execution results are attributed to the inspected candidate log and author-owned evidence. Historical dependency dispositions retain their responsible owner and exact scope; no result covers unknown customer repositories or hosted outcomes."
  ],
  "rationale": [
    "Spec alignment — pass. The retirement proposal and accepted proposal-review select bounded operational removal while preserving historical bytes and explicit dependency disposition. The current eight-model Design package directly defines v3 storage, independent transport domains, bounded archival recognition and responsible reliance. The implementation matches that selected boundary, including the prior corrected per-kind archive headers. The documentation consolidation resolves conflicting old operational language without creating new behavior or copying status, findings or evidence into explanation fields. The final expanded correction also reconciles Skill pilot recording, Design marker rollback and governed-resource context, and Test historical-adoption/evidence wording. Their current owner references agree with the canonical procedures; independent reassessment explicitly resolved design-consolidation-f1 before this final conclusion.",
    "Architecture and integrated implementation — pass. M1 detaches strict JSON decoding and v3 initialization from the retired adapter before M2 removes it. In the final code, advanced requests, targeted mutations, queries and discovery share the bounded decoder; store construction, snapshot dispatch and journal recovery select v3 consistently. Repository lifecycle and selector callers use the same header classifier, including its Git-tree reader, rather than separate legacy semantic validators. System composes these responsibilities while Record Format, CLI, Workflow and Review and Closeout retain their local authority.",
    "Test coverage — pass within the selected scope. Reviewed retained fixture/adoption/persistence and interaction assertions rather than treating reduced test counts as proof. Shared cases were retargeted before exclusive-v2 cases/resources were removed. The retained suite still protects byte/depth/Unicode/path bounds, closed vocabulary, stale revisions, explicit read basis, no-op preservation, writer exclusion and malicious or third-state recovery. No new retirement/rejection/archive-compatibility cases or disguised manual substitutes were added; static inspection of retired branches is explicitly distinguished from executable coverage.",
    "Edge cases and error handling — pass. During this fresh final review invocation, ran node --test packages/rigorloop/test/record-store-interactions.test.js packages/rigorloop/test/record-store-v3-adoption.test.js: 14/14 passed on c502e146 engineering. The subsequent ff914115/ff9154a6 changes affect only three additional model prose consumers; test, runtime, dependency, schema and package input identities remain unchanged. The test observations still establish the same current contract outcomes and no freshness override requires repeating them. Inspected their oracles and entry paths: complete advanced/targeted interaction semantics, explicit applicability transitions, public creation, advanced-to-targeted named reads/edits, stale conflict and semantic retry, and interrupted multi-record publication followed by public recovery. The recovery cases retain exact restore bytes, complete both values, and reject restore after committed state. Prior direct shared-safety proof is affirmatively reusable because no runtime/test/dependency bytes changed after the reviewed M2 source; the fresh final-source composition evidence also covers the complete candidate.",
    "Compatibility and representation — pass. Stored schema3 remains separate from targeted request1, advanced request2, advanced result1 and schema2 discovery/early responses. The final query and mutation profiles remove operational v2 acceptance while retaining accurate new-set early tags and ordinary/batch pre-selection tags. Named Review/Verify reads retain explicit omissions, optional absence and record applicability; full Finding and its six-field summary contain no origin metadata, while blockers retain origin. Complete Verify omission still removes optional verification_basis and reports the changed field. Explanation updates preserve findings and cannot silently retarget assessment basis or renew reliance.",
    "Security and privacy — pass. The shared path retains filesystem containment, safe Git modes and resolved commit checks, bounded reads/traversal, exact revision identities, lock exclusion and recovery ownership. Archive recognition uses manifest format/identity fields and supporting version/change fields, never assessment meaning, and does not hide malformed current stores, mixed reserved content or transaction residue. Errors remain bounded without exposing arbitrary request prose. No network, authentication, publication or destructive-action authority is broadened by the change.",
    "Derived artifacts and published consumers — pass for the delivered scope. Removed adapter/schema/template dependencies agree with build inputs and canonical/bundled targeted schemas. Runtime help and repository validation/discovery callers describe current v3 storage while retaining independent document/transport contracts. Canonical skills and shared recording resources retain useful trigger, ownership, prerequisites, targeted commands, proof limits, stop rules and handoff procedures; retirement removes operational v2 instructions without granting historical approvals current execution authority. Verify retains conditional Git basis and success-only final assessment; PR retains separate external authority. Final-source package/selector/broad-smoke evidence supports the composed distribution surface, not customer installation or publication.",
    "Historical preservation and scope — pass. TG-00 supplies the responsible pre-removal work/recovery/governance disposition and exact inspected evidence, with historical limitations and external unknowns retained. No other change directory differs from the original base. Old example JSON bytes remain unchanged, and current indexes clearly separate archival illustrations. The consolidation changes only seventeen Design/navigation files beyond the M2 engineering source; later suffix changes only stage evidence. Stable model requirement/decision identities and current source ownership remain coherent. There is no unrelated feature, permanent compatibility reader, migration or renewed historical approval.",
    "Validation evidence — pass. Inspected the final-source repository CI log, whose recorded source is ff9154a661183a88ee0afbb17330761b2c6d4c58, prepared revision 012bc6b696de33c3310cc60c6130ee0191562e8a and candidate 7c808a76d09073e586bbcc62928c23374f0ace58fd7a7a54a83973d83374b11b. It reports selected checks passed, including model/schema, guidance, lifecycle/metadata, selector, package and trigger-owned broad smoke. This is attributed local candidate evidence, not hosted CI. Earlier M1/M2 recording/package/Python results remain evidence for unchanged proved surfaces; the final-source CI reruns composition against the consolidated documents. The fresh independent 14-case execution is separately identified rather than presented as the complete plan run.",
    "Final integration and authority — pass. Current context has both implementation milestones completed, both owned Design findings resolved and no selected open blocker. The new current Design assessment explicitly finds the unchanged Delivery allocation applicable to documentation consolidation; no new runtime requirement or verification family emerged. Earlier Design/final Code Review records are explicitly stale for changed documentation and are not used as present approval. This review freshly assesses the whole source diff, exact current subjects and cross-milestone interactions. Its outcome supports a distinct Verify assessment; it does not replace Verify or select workflow activity."
  ],
